# Storyboard v2. One line per composition:
#   beats | on screen | what this moment is for | how it leaves | carried into next shot
# "## N Title | target" starts a chapter. 1 beat = 0.75 s (80 BPM). Scale tags: CLOSE, WIDE, OVER (map/overhead
# diagram view), FULL (full-frame type), 3D. [SIG1] [SIG2] [SIG3] mark the three signature moments.
# Persistent objects: CHIP (gold patch.diff), LOOP (agent loop: think → call a tool → read the result, exit
# branch submit_patch), CONT (container silhouette: rounded case with a header strip; A blue, B green), TAPE
# (context window), GRID (task cells), TREE (bundle file tree), RAIL (HUD chapter tag).

## 0 Cold open | 80
4 | CLOSE frame one, finished: issue card fills the frame — header "Issue · open", corner tag "illustrative example", title `summarize([]) raises ZeroDivisionError`, body "Expected 0 for an empty list." | hook with something every engineer recognises | card slides left and shrinks while a code panel draws in from the right | issue card
